<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mu'nis al-Muzaffar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 845–<a href="/years/933">933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Mu'nis al-Khadim, Abu'l-Hasan Mu'nis al-Qushuri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mu'nis al-Muzaffar, also called al-Khadim, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">Eunuch</a>, was commander-in-chief of the Abbasid army from 908 until his death in 933 and virtual dictator and king-maker of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> from 928. A Byzantine Greek eunuch slave, he served the future caliph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid">al-Mu'tadid</a> from the 880s, was banished to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 901, and was recalled in 908 by al-Muqtadir, whom he saved from a palace coup that December. He raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, defeated Fatimid invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 915 and 920 and saved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarmatians">Qarmatians</a> in 927. After a confrontation in 931–932 that ended with al-Muqtadir's death in battle, he installed al-Qahir, who had him executed in August 933.</p></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.32,44.37&amp;year=902" aria-label="Baghdad on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5684 954 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Mu'nis al-Muzaffar"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6134 1224h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=33.32,44.37&amp;year=902">What was here in 902 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
